📧 HR Email Automation

An AI-powered HR email processing workflow built with n8n, Gmail, OpenAI, Google Sheets, and Turbo.

The workflow monitors incoming HR emails, validates the message flow, classifies each request with AI, and routes it to the appropriate automated HR process.

✨ What it does

Monitors the Gmail inbox every minute.

Ignores email threads that are not new incoming requests.

Filters for Turbo-related emails before classification.

Uses an AI text classifier to identify the request category.

Creates the appropriate task card in the Turbo platform.

Builds process-specific checklists and rules.

Generates professional email acknowledgements in Arabic or English.

Extracts structured employee and shortage data for shortage cases.

Stores shortage information in Google Sheets.

Supports separate automation paths for multiple HR request types.

🧠 Classification & Routing

The workflow defines these AI categories:

Category

Automation

department_transfer

Transfer task + rules/steps checklist + confirmation

resign

Resignation + exit interview + clearance/policy checklists + confirmation

robbery

Theft/shortage case + checklist + employee/shortage extraction + Sheets logging + reply

recruitment

Recruitment task + intake/hiring/rules checklists + acknowledgement

promotion

Promotion task + review/rules checklists + confirmation

investigation

Investigation task + investigation checklist + confirmation

advance_request

Advance request task + checklist + confirmation

undefined

Fallback task + fallback reply

The classifier also contains definitions for shifting_job and Custody Request, but these routes are not connected in the current workflow export. They should be treated as future extensions rather than implemented features.

